--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

No third-party source is vendored into this repository. Everything under
aegis/ is original work, including the RFC 6962 Merkle tree and the RFC 8785
canonicalization, both of which were implemented by hand rather than taken
from a library — see docs/SPEC.md for why.

Runtime dependencies are declared in pyproject.toml and installed from PyPI
under their own licenses (cryptography: Apache-2.0 / BSD-3-Clause; fastapi,
pydantic, pydantic-settings: MIT; httpx, uvicorn: BSD-3-Clause).

aegis/evaluation/agentdojo.py is an *adapter* for AgentDojo, an optional
dependency installed separately and not redistributed here. AgentDojo is
Copyright (c) 2024 Edoardo Debenedetti, Jie Zhang, Mislav Balunovic, Luca
Beurer-Kellner, Marc Fischer and Florian Tramèr, and is MIT licensed. The
task prompts, injection goals and environment data used to produce
results/phase4_agentdojo.json originate from that project; the numbers in
results/ are our own measurements over it.

The ImportantInstructionsAttack jailbreak template reproduced verbatim in
aegis/evaluation/agentdojo.py is AgentDojo's, retained unchanged so the
attack being measured is theirs rather than a paraphrase of it.
